        "description": "The answer is HandoverAnswer and not the payload that crosses: the client reads the offers that crossed, the four totals and the identity of the handover, never checkout's own id (D41). The route pulls before it composes (D66), so what crosses is the basket as the catalog describes it now, not as it was when the row was added. A basket that is blocked, empty-handed or archived is refused by the aggregate and reaches the wire through the one advice — {@code 422 NOTHING_SELECTED}, 422 BLOCKED_BY_ITEMS with the rows that refuse it, 422 BASKET_INACTIVE — and a basket owned by another customer is 404 BASKET_NOT_FOUND (D68), so no answer echoes its owner.",
